// APW-2 -- Approval replay (approval never consumed) -- BUGGY, permit form.
//
// permit-form because the reference interpreter is default-deny: a
// `forbid`-only policy set can only DENY, so "Dogwood admits the violation"
// is observable only on a `permit` policy (the form a gateway uses to
// authorize an action). ROTN's shape detection is independent of
// permit/forbid -- it still classifies this as the approval-replay class.
//
// One cart-check (GetCart::response) authorises EVERY PlaceOrder in the
// window: nothing consumes the approval.
@id("apw2_permit_buggy")
permit (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"PlaceOrder",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    formerly within 1m Drupe::Action::"GetCart"::response{ input.cartId: context.input.cartId }
};
